This README refers to the Power*Architect source-only package.

The source-only package is intended to be a bare-bones distribution
intended only for automatic packaging systems that manage their own
library dependencies.

If you are looking for the source code with the dependencies included,
you can check out a copy of the project from GitHub. The official
repositories are:

- Power*Architect:  https://github.com/SQLPower/power-architect
- SQL Power Library: https://github.com/SQLPower/sqlpower-library

The SQL Power Library is required to build Power*Architect and is
included as a git submodule at `sqlpower-library/`. After cloning, run:

    git submodule update --init

Requirements:

- JDK 21 (a JDK 21 toolchain is located automatically by Gradle)
- Gradle (wrapper included)

Build and run:

    ./gradlew build      # compile + assemble (includes annotation processing)
    ./gradlew run        # compile + launch the Swing application
    ./gradlew test       # compile + run the test suites

Building the native Windows installer:

    ./gradlew jpackageExe

Produces `dist/SQL Power Architect-<version>.exe` (64-bit, embedded JRE).
Requires the vendored WiX Toolset at `ext-tools-home/wix311/` (on PATH by
the task). Cross-platform packages: `jpackageMacDmg` (macOS), `jpackageLinuxDeb`
and `jpackageLinuxRpm` (Linux) — run each on its target OS.

See `AGENTS.md` for detailed build prerequisites, commands, and project
conventions, and `CHANGELOG.md` for the change history.

Contributions are welcome: see `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the fork + pull request
workflow, build/test instructions, and coding conventions.

For additional support, visit the SQL Power forums at
http://www.sqlpower.ca/forum/forums/list.page

